  "body": "## What changed\n- `crates/motion/src/machining2d/lead_fit.rs`: a new function `seam_tangents` gives the lead-in and lead-out tangents. `plan_leads` and `both_fit` use it.\n- On a closed ring, it compares the start tangent and the end tangent at the seam.\n- If the ring bends to the air side at the seam, the lead-out tangent is mirrored across the start tangent. The lead-in tangent is mirrored across the end tangent.\n- Then each lead leaves the seam on the air side of the whole ring.\n- A smooth seam, a seam that bends away from the air, and an open walk (tab windows, chains, an exit point) keep their tangents.\n- New test file `crates/motion/tests/contour_tab_lead.rs`.\n- Decision record `docs/decisions/3019-contour-tab-lead-cross.md`.\n\n## Cause\n- The seam of a round-cornered outside ring falls on a fitted corner arc.\n- The arc's end tangent is about 0.05 degree off the ring's first chord, toward the material.\n- The 8 mm linear lead-out goes along that tangent. It crosses the ring's second move about 0.25 mm past the seam.\n- The crossing law found this on each level. This is the issue's \"feed moves 5 and 13 cross\" (one pair on each level).\n- Tabs are not the cause. The same crossing occurs with no tabs.\n- On a conventional cut, the lead-in has the same fault against the ring's last move.\n- The crossing law is correct and does not change.\n\n## Tests\nPins (the issue's plate: 120 x 80, four R6 corners, D10 tool, stepdown 3, 12 deep, 4 tabs 3 x 1, linear lead 8):\n- `an_outside_tabbed_contour_with_a_linear_lead_has_no_crossing` (climb, 4 tabs).\n- `an_outside_contour_with_a_linear_lead_has_no_crossing_with_or_without_tabs` (climb with no tabs; conventional with 0 and 4 tabs).\n- Each case asserts: no `crossed_pairs`, no `Crossing` or `Gouge` from `verify`, and a full 8 mm lead-in and lead-out.\n\nRed before the fix: yes, both pins. Failure text: `feed crossings [[5, 14], [21, 30], [37, 46], [53, 62]]`.\n\nMutations:\n- Old `lead_fit.rs` from upstream/main: both pins red.\n- Lead-in mirror removed: the conventional case red (`[[3, 12], [19, 28], [35, 44], [51, 60]]`).\n- Lead-out mirror removed: both pins red.\n- Fix restored: both pins green.\n\nGate:\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green (motion lib, climb_direction, contour_tab_lead, one_descent).\n- Also run: motion `contour_start`, `machining2d`, `contour_tabs`, `contour_tab_bridge`, `contour_tab_height`, `contour_tab_necks`, `control_comp`. All green.\n- Also run: app `golden_cl`, `conformance`, `control_comp`, `solid_law_goldens`, `microarc_test_part`, `corner_relief`, `verify`. All green.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\nNone.\n\n## Not exercised\n- The QA project file of the issue (`q01-blocked.camproj`) was not opened. The pin rebuilds the same plate and operation in `camcraft-motion`.\n- `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main` was not run. A run is necessary before the PR is flagged ready.\n- Inside contours (bores) with a bend at the seam. The law uses the air side, so it applies to them too. No pin covers them.\n\n## Overlaps\nNone. No open PR changes `lead_fit.rs`.\n\nChangelog: A 2D Contour with a linear lead on a part with round corners no longer gets a lead-in or lead-out that crosses the cut at the seam, so verify does not hold the post.\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #3019\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
